1
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:46,990
We'll be right back.

2
00:01:47,010 --> 00:02:16,990
We'll be right back.

3
00:02:17,010 --> 00:02:46,990
We'll be right back.

4
00:02:47,010 --> 00:02:51,950
Spondum Ski, the day the sea train shook.

5
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:58,950
Spondum Ski, the day the sea train shook.

6
00:02:59,950 --> 00:03:00,810
Interesting.

7
00:03:01,690 --> 00:03:04,830
Many ships were born in this cobwebbed room.

8
00:03:05,410 --> 00:03:06,490
And now look at it.

9
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:07,710
Filthy.

10
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:11,830
They built ships here?

11
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:20,310
Tom, Iceberg, and Cutty Flam.

12
00:03:21,110 --> 00:03:25,770
This place must hold countless memories of days when you still shared a life with those two.

13
00:03:25,770 --> 00:03:30,570
And now you call it your top secret base.

14
00:03:30,930 --> 00:03:32,950
That's heartbreakingly adorable.

15
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:34,710
Damn you.

16
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:37,370
Just get the hell out of here already.

17
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:40,310
We won't leave till we get what we're after.

18
00:03:40,850 --> 00:03:42,910
Make this easy on yourself.

19
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:45,090
There ain't no blueprints in here.

20
00:03:45,950 --> 00:03:46,990
Oh, no?

21
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:48,630
You don't say.

22
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:51,110
Hey!

23
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:51,910
Califa!

24
00:03:51,910 --> 00:04:00,630
Oh, damn it!

25
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:05,410
Just keep it together, Usopp!

26
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:10,970
You bastard!

27
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:15,350
Take your time, but be aware that we know many things about your past.

28
00:04:15,550 --> 00:04:17,250
Things that you don't want getting out.

29
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:20,270
For example, we know what happened eight years ago.

30
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:24,010
And that you are guilty of committing a very serious crime back then.

31
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:26,210
Just like your dear old Tom.

32
00:04:26,210 --> 00:04:27,190
You shut up!

33
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:28,910
Tom was never a damn criminal!

34
00:04:29,270 --> 00:04:31,650
You don't know what the hell you're talking about!

35
00:04:31,870 --> 00:04:32,730
You freak!

36
00:04:42,090 --> 00:04:42,650
Tom!

37
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:47,150
Stay back!

38
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:48,930
I disagree.

39
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:50,870
You're both criminals.

40
00:04:50,870 --> 00:04:55,310
And as such, you should be made to feel the consequences of your actions.

41
00:04:55,310 --> 00:05:00,290
Frankie, whatever happens, don't interfere with what I'm about to do.

42
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:01,570
No matter what.

43
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,670
You talk like you know everything.

44
00:05:05,370 --> 00:05:07,150
You don't know Tom.

45
00:05:08,550 --> 00:05:12,170
And you don't know anything about Water 7!

46
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:25,870
I heard the judicial ship will be here in three days.

47
00:05:26,030 --> 00:05:28,450
Finally putting Tom on trial, are they?

48
00:05:28,650 --> 00:05:30,110
I hope it ends well for him.

49
00:05:30,490 --> 00:05:31,870
I'm sure it will.

50
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:32,870
Right.

51
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:35,730
He fulfilled his promise, after all.

52
00:05:36,230 --> 00:05:37,450
That he did.

53
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:42,850
All right, let's get that lumber in the dock.

54
00:05:43,570 --> 00:05:45,970
So, how'd the deal work out with St. Poplar?

55
00:05:46,210 --> 00:05:47,170
Not that great.

56
00:05:47,370 --> 00:05:50,450
They're taking advantage of us since we don't have much to trade with them.

57
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:52,970
Like iron from San Valdo.

58
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:55,710
We'll all be in the red if this kind of crap keeps up.

59
00:05:56,070 --> 00:05:58,910
We're not gonna let this keep happening now, are we guys?

60
00:05:59,650 --> 00:06:00,090
Yeah!

61
00:06:00,090 --> 00:06:01,650
No way!

62
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:09,550
The people do seem to be happy about being able to cross the ocean.

63
00:06:09,930 --> 00:06:12,890
But they say the trade situation isn't as good as they'd hoped.

64
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:16,110
I wonder if this town needs more than a sea train.

65
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:18,590
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

66
00:06:18,850 --> 00:06:20,730
Ah, but the spirits are up, boy!

67
00:06:20,990 --> 00:06:23,950
That's a major step, so give the rest some time.

68
00:06:24,230 --> 00:06:26,310
We've done our best, so be proud.

69
00:06:26,450 --> 00:06:28,790
Keep your head held high and walk with gusto!

70
00:06:28,790 --> 00:06:29,130
Let's go!

71
00:06:29,670 --> 00:06:30,070
Yeah.

72
00:06:40,050 --> 00:06:41,170
You there!

73
00:06:41,470 --> 00:06:45,290
Am I correct in assuming I'm speaking with Mr. Tom, the shipbuilding engineer?

74
00:06:45,790 --> 00:06:47,750
You're a difficult man to pin down.

75
00:06:48,130 --> 00:06:48,490
Hmm?

76
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:51,630
I have some matter of great importance I wish to...

77
00:06:51,630 --> 00:06:51,970
Um, sir?

78
00:06:52,150 --> 00:06:53,470
This man and I are talking!

79
00:06:53,790 --> 00:06:54,310
Yes, sir!

80
00:06:54,510 --> 00:06:56,790
Again, before I was so rudely...

81
00:06:56,790 --> 00:06:56,950
Hmm?

82
00:06:58,790 --> 00:07:08,510
I was going to say, my name is Agent Spondum from Cypher Pole number five!

83
00:07:08,930 --> 00:07:09,810
Stop it, sir!

84
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:12,350
Ha ha ha ha ha!

85
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:12,990
Wow!

86
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:14,550
Sorry about that!

87
00:07:14,730 --> 00:07:15,430
My bad!

88
00:07:15,930 --> 00:07:18,570
Looks like you got in the way of my victory cannon salute!

89
00:07:18,990 --> 00:07:19,690
Tough luck!

90
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:21,990
It's super!

91
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:25,110
Battle Frankie 35 comes home with booty!

92
00:07:25,330 --> 00:07:25,990
That's right!

93
00:07:26,150 --> 00:07:27,190
Check it out!

94
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:31,290
Is this not the biggest sea king you ever laid your eyes on?

95
00:07:31,570 --> 00:07:32,410
Ha ha ha ha!

96
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:34,490
I can't believe him.

97
00:07:34,730 --> 00:07:36,170
I'm still acting like a child.

98
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:38,770
Hey!

99
00:07:39,030 --> 00:07:41,590
What the hell do you think you're doing, ice for brains?

100
00:07:42,130 --> 00:07:42,390
Oh!

101
00:07:42,950 --> 00:07:44,590
Will you ever grow up?

102
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:47,990
Ever since you were a kid, all you want to do is build these stupid battleships.

103
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:49,490
It's time to stop.

104
00:07:49,830 --> 00:07:53,730
This better be the last one, or I'm going to start tearing them all apart myself.

105
00:07:53,730 --> 00:07:58,510
Want a vet? You lay a finger on my ship, and you'll draw back a stump, you hear me?

106
00:07:58,630 --> 00:08:04,090
Yeah? Well, listen, Frankie, if you were able to kill a sea king with this floating piece of junk,

107
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:05,670
that means it's a dangerous weapon.

108
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:09,110
And you've got all those other battleships of yours just strewn around here?

109
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:09,890
What are you thinking?

110
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:12,890
Hey, it's not like I'm attacking people with them, am I?

111
00:08:13,330 --> 00:08:18,410
I'm not saying you do that, but you're making it easier for anyone else who'd want to, you idiot.

112
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:25,750
Am I right? Back me up here, Tom.

113
00:08:26,270 --> 00:08:28,670
Flunky's weapons are going to be the end of our business.

114
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:31,870
Flunky, that's rich.

115
00:08:32,370 --> 00:08:34,770
Hold on, this is no laughing matter.

116
00:08:35,090 --> 00:08:39,510
I demand a sincere apology and that you listen to what I've come here to say.

117
00:08:40,050 --> 00:08:43,690
Government guy, are you? So, is this about the trial?

118
00:08:44,110 --> 00:08:46,290
Trial? What the devil are you talking about?

119
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:49,730
No, this concerns an altogether different matter.

120
00:08:50,270 --> 00:08:52,810
Oh, now what?

121
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:57,570
Did Tom come back with you boys?

122
00:08:57,850 --> 00:08:59,290
No, I think he's with a visitor.

123
00:09:00,270 --> 00:09:01,570
Some man from the government.

124
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:03,130
It wasn't about the trial.

125
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:05,350
Spawn, spawn something.

126
00:09:06,030 --> 00:09:07,870
Spawn something dumb, maybe?

127
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:08,690
How strange.

128
00:09:09,010 --> 00:09:10,730
And he's not from the judicial ship?

129
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:13,290
The government is so disorganized.

130
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:20,050
Afraid not. I've got no blueprints for something like that.

131
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:22,230
That's nonsense.

132
00:09:22,650 --> 00:09:24,850
Do you take me for some kind of weak-minded simpleton?

133
00:09:25,190 --> 00:09:27,990
I researched the history of Water 7 for countless hours.

134
00:09:28,230 --> 00:09:31,890
And I am absolutely certain this document can only be in your possession.

135
00:09:31,890 --> 00:09:37,610
You're saying that you actually have the authority to investigate me?

136
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,590
That's right, I do.

137
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:45,570
And what's more, I learned all about your dealings with Gold Roger in the course of my investigation.

138
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:50,170
So unless you want me to share that information with my colleagues, you're going to cooperate.

139
00:09:50,410 --> 00:09:53,370
Why would I care? The government already knows about it.

140
00:09:53,370 --> 00:09:53,890
We do?

141
00:09:53,890 --> 00:09:55,830
That's such a poppycock.

142
00:09:56,150 --> 00:10:00,590
If that's true, why are you here and not rotting away somewhere in a jail cell?

143
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:03,730
Use your investigative powers and find out for yourself.

144
00:10:03,990 --> 00:10:04,510
Good day.

145
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:08,450
Hey, you can't treat a government agent like this.

146
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:10,210
Open this door immediately.

147
00:10:13,210 --> 00:10:14,190
That's right.

148
00:10:14,470 --> 00:10:15,430
It's all true.

149
00:10:15,770 --> 00:10:16,650
Yes, sir.

150
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:19,250
He did exactly what he told the judge he'd do.

151
00:10:19,250 --> 00:10:23,210
And they should be dropping the charges at the trial that's coming up.

152
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:25,990
That man saved this island for sure.

153
00:10:26,290 --> 00:10:31,170
It makes my blood boil to think that damn criminal is being treated like a hero.

154
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:33,130
I see.

155
00:10:33,570 --> 00:10:36,430
You're certain that such a thing truly exists?

156
00:10:36,670 --> 00:10:37,490
Yes, sir.

157
00:10:37,650 --> 00:10:40,670
And the pirates are scouring the globe for it as we speak.

158
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:43,410
That's why it's imperative we locate it immediately.

159
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:47,850
If it were to fall into the wrong hands, the resulting destruction would be inconceivable.

160
00:10:47,850 --> 00:10:52,050
We've been suffering through this great pirate era for more than a decade now.

161
00:10:52,230 --> 00:10:55,490
It's a vile sickness that grows worse with every passing day.

162
00:10:55,770 --> 00:10:57,550
The time for idle discussion is over.

163
00:10:57,830 --> 00:11:00,190
We must do more than to prevent this weapon's construction.

164
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:03,870
We must build it ourselves and use it as a mighty instrument of justice.

165
00:11:04,270 --> 00:11:08,810
With it, we can eliminate this pirate scourge and bring law and order back to our land.

166
00:11:10,810 --> 00:11:13,150
This is indeed a troubling error.

167
00:11:13,470 --> 00:11:14,970
There's no doubt about that.

168
00:11:14,970 --> 00:11:18,850
Your primary objective will be to locate and then obtain these blueprints.

169
00:11:19,110 --> 00:11:20,510
That will be all at this time.

170
00:11:20,810 --> 00:11:24,050
We trust that you can complete this mission, Spondum.

171
00:11:24,630 --> 00:11:26,350
Yes, sir. Without fail.

172
00:11:27,550 --> 00:11:31,630
I've been working on this case for far too long to see it all go up in smoke.

173
00:11:31,890 --> 00:11:33,890
It's right within my grasp now.

174
00:11:33,890 --> 00:11:38,890
Let's go.

175
00:11:42,890 --> 00:11:47,670
If the judge decides to acquit him, that'll mean a real headache for me.

176
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:49,670
Spondum, sir!

177
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:59,730
The charge will stick, and that bastard will hang.

178
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:03,930
Men, I'll need five more agents, stat!

179
00:12:04,130 --> 00:12:04,310
Hmm.

180
00:12:09,590 --> 00:12:11,130
Spondum, sir!

181
00:12:11,130 --> 00:12:38,710
Iceberg, Frankie.

182
00:12:39,050 --> 00:12:39,370
Yeah?

183
00:12:39,370 --> 00:12:40,910
Hey, boys, come here.

184
00:12:41,270 --> 00:12:41,770
What's up?

185
00:12:42,090 --> 00:12:44,670
It's about time I let you in on something important.

186
00:12:45,410 --> 00:12:45,650
Hmm.

187
00:12:50,350 --> 00:12:53,510
Why would anyone even dream of something like this?

188
00:12:54,230 --> 00:12:55,590
Is this for real?

189
00:12:55,770 --> 00:12:57,350
Can this thing actually be built?

190
00:12:57,650 --> 00:12:59,650
Those are the blueprints for a nightmare.

191
00:12:59,970 --> 00:13:00,950
A real monster.

192
00:13:01,350 --> 00:13:05,270
The government has learned of their existence and has started sniffing around for them.

193
00:13:05,270 --> 00:13:07,830
It's too dangerous for me to keep them anymore.

194
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:10,750
This is terrifying, but I agree.

195
00:13:11,330 --> 00:13:12,090
I'll keep them.

196
00:13:13,870 --> 00:13:14,410
Iceberg!

197
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:17,030
Hey, let's see if we can build this thing!

198
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:17,930
You idiot!

199
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:18,270
Ow!

200
00:13:18,270 --> 00:13:23,950
Do you ever think before you speak, this thing can never be built?

201
00:13:24,310 --> 00:13:26,870
Do you realize how much destruction it could cause?

202
00:13:26,870 --> 00:13:28,130
Huh?

203
00:13:28,130 --> 00:13:28,210
Huh?

204
00:13:28,210 --> 00:13:28,710
Hmm.

205
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:29,210
Hmm.

206
00:13:29,210 --> 00:13:29,710
Hmm.

207
00:13:31,710 --> 00:13:32,050
Yeah.

208
00:13:32,050 --> 00:13:34,010
The world would be done for.

209
00:13:36,170 --> 00:13:38,330
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

210
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:42,490
Besides trying to build the damn thing, you can do whatever the hell you want with it for now.

211
00:13:42,570 --> 00:13:43,970
Even toss it if you need to.

212
00:13:44,310 --> 00:13:45,330
Yes, of course.

213
00:13:46,010 --> 00:13:47,330
Well, I got your attention.

214
00:13:48,510 --> 00:13:50,870
Here's another storm a-brewin'.

215
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:58,630
Frankie, hold on.

216
00:13:58,630 --> 00:13:58,990
Ah.

217
00:14:00,290 --> 00:14:01,150
For what?

218
00:14:02,010 --> 00:14:04,090
For your pants, you silly boy.

219
00:14:04,290 --> 00:14:08,790
I swear, you'd think after all that attention you got last time you went out dressed like that,

220
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:10,670
you'd be wise enough not to do it again.

221
00:14:11,030 --> 00:14:13,410
Jeez, I'm just going out to get a few things.

222
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:14,250
Ha, ha, ha.

223
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:16,370
Now that you're dressed, you can skeedaddle.

224
00:14:16,370 --> 00:14:17,250
Thanks.

225
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:22,630
Can't believe she's making a big dinner just because the stupid judge is finally saying Tom's not guilty.

226
00:14:22,990 --> 00:14:24,230
Never was in the first place.

227
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:26,170
Ha, ha, ha.

228
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:26,690
All right.

229
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:29,830
Rise and shine!

230
00:14:30,790 --> 00:14:33,030
Tom, iceberg, give up!

231
00:14:33,690 --> 00:14:34,950
Today's judgment day.

232
00:14:35,110 --> 00:14:36,850
Don't want to sleep through your big trial.

233
00:14:39,850 --> 00:14:41,330
Let's get down to the harbor!

234
00:14:41,530 --> 00:14:43,370
They're gonna hand down Tom's sentence!

235
00:14:46,370 --> 00:14:53,810
The spectators are boarding the ship in droves.

236
00:14:54,470 --> 00:14:55,890
The people are really interested.

237
00:14:56,210 --> 00:14:57,510
Seems like it'll be a big trial.

238
00:14:57,870 --> 00:14:58,850
Seems that way.

239
00:14:59,430 --> 00:15:01,910
Have you had a chance to see the sea train yet, Your Honor?

240
00:15:02,070 --> 00:15:02,270
Hmm.

241
00:15:02,750 --> 00:15:03,830
I have indeed.

242
00:15:04,130 --> 00:15:04,930
Quite impressive.

243
00:15:05,350 --> 00:15:07,130
A true feat of ingenuity.

244
00:15:07,710 --> 00:15:09,430
He fulfilled his end of the bargain.

245
00:15:09,850 --> 00:15:13,350
I'm certain the people will rejoice to see their hero go free.

246
00:15:14,110 --> 00:15:15,390
Is Tom here yet?

247
00:15:15,390 --> 00:15:16,530
I wish I could start already.

248
00:15:17,350 --> 00:15:18,070
Come on.

249
00:15:18,130 --> 00:15:19,890
We gotta hurry before all the seats are taken.

250
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:20,550
I know.

251
00:15:20,650 --> 00:15:23,410
I can't wait to see the look on his face when the judge lets him off.

252
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:24,530
What a trip.

253
00:15:25,410 --> 00:15:25,850
Wow.

254
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:28,010
Can't believe it's been 14 years.

255
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:41,770
That ship's under attack!

256
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:50,970
Get away from it!

257
00:15:51,330 --> 00:15:52,050
Hooray!

258
00:15:52,050 --> 00:15:52,830
What the?

259
00:15:52,830 --> 00:15:54,610
Is this a pirate raid?

260
00:15:54,610 --> 00:15:58,070
But how?

261
00:15:58,610 --> 00:16:00,730
Where is this attack even coming from?

262
00:16:00,850 --> 00:16:01,570
Hey, look!

263
00:16:01,790 --> 00:16:02,650
Over there!

264
00:16:03,210 --> 00:16:03,930
What?

265
00:16:04,070 --> 00:16:05,130
Some kind of fleet!

266
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:13,610
Those look like battleships.

267
00:16:13,910 --> 00:16:15,490
Those pirates are attacking us!

268
00:16:15,490 --> 00:16:18,610
